Subject: [amelia] Is there a way to specify interaction effects when imputing missing data?
In-Reply-To: <a6f585d20910080536r5b183468xd4797841eb106d74@mail.gmail.com>
References: <a6f585d20910072150t667e6ff0lef76ffef1953f90d@mail.gmail.com> <a6f585d20910080536r5b183468xd4797841eb106d74@mail.gmail.com>
Message-ID: <839691710910080550s6fdedc0fj96c9d181a8d1ca16@mail.gmail.com>

Hi Donald,

Amelia does not have an option for imputing interactions currently.
You should definitely include interaction terms in your imputation
model if you need to (it's in your analysis model or it's an important
predictor of missingness). However, if you need to use that variable
subsequently, you should replace the imputation of the interaction
with the interaction of the imputations.

I hope this helps,
matt.

